SPEAR documentation
======================

Sphinx documentation for SPEAR. The configuration is the one shared by its
sibling projects' documentation, taken verbatim so the manuals build and
look the same: doc/Makefile, sources in doc/source/*.rst,
configuration in doc/source/conf.py, theme overrides in
doc/source/_static/theme_overrides.css, output in doc/build/ (generated —
never edit it, never index it).

Only these differ from the shared configuration:

  * conf.py: project, copyright, LaTeX/man titles, and the version string
    (see below);
  * requirements.txt: sphinxcontrib-plantuml added (conf.py loads it;
    the sibling projects get it from their CI image), sphinxcontrib-pdfembed dropped
    (not on PyPI, so the GitHub runner cannot install it);
  * doc/utils/plantuml.jar (22 MB) is not versioned: conf.py loads the
    plantuml extension as the siblings do, but no page uses the `uml`
    directive. The day one does, copy the jar from a sibling's doc/utils/
    (it is gitignored here) and decide how CI gets it;
  * CI is .github/workflows/docs.yml (GitHub Pages) instead of
    doc/.gitlab-ci.yml, with the same `sphinx-build -W --keep-going` line.

When the shared configuration changes, copy the file over and re-apply
the differences above. Do not add project-specific styling or options.

Structure
---------

index.rst follows the shared landing page: the REDS/HEIG-VD logotype
centred, one hidden numbered toctree, a centred title, and left-aligned
sections that list :ref: links. Prose belongs in the chapters, not on the
landing page.

A topic with several pages gets a directory and an eponymous index
(harness/harness.rst, model/model.rst). Every page carries a label
(`.. _name:` above its title) so references to it are :ref: and break the
build if their target disappears.

Cross-references are absolute (:doc:`/harness/sandbox`), and so are image
paths from a subdirectory (/img/...). A relative reference changes meaning
with the directory of the page that writes it.

Warnings are errors
-------------------

CI builds with `sphinx-build -W --keep-going`. Without -W, an extension that
cannot reach its native tool only logs a warning and drops the node: the job
stays green while the diagrams are missing from the published pages.

To check warnings reliably, clean first — an incremental build skips the
consistency check:

    make clean && make html

Build
-----

    make html                 # -> build/html/index.html
    make latexpdf             # -> build/latex/SPEAR.pdf
    make clean

Sphinx and the RTD theme come from the system Python (/usr/bin/sphinx-build),
not from the spear virtualenv, which carries only the application's
runtime dependencies.

Diagrams
--------

As in the sibling projects: source/img/SPEAR.drawio holds every diagram, one page
each, and is edited directly in draw.io. Each page the documentation uses is
exported to source/img/SPEAR-<Page>.drawio.png and committed with the
.drawio in the same change; the .rst files reference the PNG
(/img/SPEAR-<Page>.drawio.png). The command-line export, and why the snap
needs the file staged under ~/snap/drawio/common, are in
source/directory_layout.rst ("This documentation").

The version string
------------------

The sibling projects derive `release` from their release tag. SPEAR has no
release tags, so conf.py derives it from spear/active-model.conf instead: the served
model appears in the page header and never has to be bumped by hand.
